# Pipeline safety

- **Fetch/queue split**: X discovery enqueues only; never wait on Bluesky media upload/post inside the sweep.
- **Destination locks**: Serialize all writes per destination; different destinations may run concurrently.
- **Queue identity**: Destination-scoped keys prevent duplicate posts to one destination; allow intentional multi-destination posts.
- **Validation is read-only**: login + session metadata only — never profile/label/pin/follow/post in validate paths.
- **Mutations need intent**: profile, bot-label, display-suffix, pin, follow, post require explicit gates — not hidden in preview/validate.
- **Auth cache**: Evict agents on auth failure and password rotate; prefer credential-aware cache keys so stale passwords are not reused.
- **Runtime health**: Record account/destination login success/failure without logging secrets.
- Queue rows keep immutable policy snapshots; re-evaluate only via explicit operator action.

Use skill `run-quality-gate` after pipeline changes. Subagent `pipeline-regression` for focused review.
